WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.135
-Hello, everyone, and welcome
back to the captain's quarters.

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:05.305
Now here at the show, we have
always been responsive

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.273
to viewer feedback
and criticism.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.676
So I'd just like to say to those
of you who are not necessarily

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:14.080
huge fans of my new sidekick
the sea captain,

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.783
we hear you and we are taking it
under advisement.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.118
Now, you should know
this negative feedback

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.619
does hurt his feelings.

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:23.790
-Sea captains are people, too.
-But as I've told him,

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.958
that's one of the hard realities
of show business.

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:28.928
-Maybe this old mariner
just wasn't cut out

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:32.132
for the rocky shores
of Hollywood.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.799
-And speaking
of deranged conversations

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:35.401
that don't go anywhere,
President Trump

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:37.737
gave a truly terrifying
interview

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.405
in which he made clear
he does not care about

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:41.341
the pandemic that's raging
out of control

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.843
as he sends secret police
to an American city

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.712
to snatch protesters
off the streets.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.581
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:52.385 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.486
The country's in the midst
of a spiraling pandemic

00:00:54.486 --> 00:00:56.689
that has killed 140,000
Americans

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.058
and left tens of millions
unemployed.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.259
And yet the president has,

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:02.195
according to Republican
officials,

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:05.097
people close to him
and our own eyes and ears

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:07.867
decide to just move on
from the crisis.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.202
An adviser to the Republican
governor of Texas

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:12.238
where the outbreak is spreading
out of control

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.306
told "The New York Times"
over the weekend,

00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:16.743
"the president
got bored with it."

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:20.646
Oh, I'm sorry, Commodus,
were you not entertained?

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:22.882
Seriously, you were bored
with the pandemic?

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.151
Bored with the quarantine,
I understand.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:28.654
I've watched so much Netflix,
the on-screen message changed.

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:30.957
But you're bored
with the pandemic?

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.291
That's your job.

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:34.360
Would you have preferred
if the coronavirus

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.562
had a swimsuit contest?

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.330
And even when he can be bothered

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.864
to talk about the coronavirus
outbreak,

00:01:38.864 --> 00:01:41.633
he can't help but immediately
veer into a topic

00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:44.370
that's more interesting to him,
like his TV ratings.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.372
Today he announced
he'd be bringing back

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:49.341
his humiliating press
briefings/therapy sessions,

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:51.477
not because there's
an out of control pandemic

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:52.611
that requires leadership,

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:55.648
but because his TV ratings
were so good.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.151 line:0%
-Well, we had very
successful briefings.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.119 line:0%
I was doing them, and, uh...

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.454 line:0%
We had a lot of people watching,

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.855 line:0%
record numbers watching.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.991 line:0%
In the history
of cable television,

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.392 line:0%
there's never been
anything like it.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.028 line:0%
So I think we'll start that
probably starting tomorrow.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.964 line:0%
I'll do it at 5:00 like
we were doing.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.700 line:0%
We had a good slot.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.201 line:0%
And a lot of people were
watching,

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.369 line:0%
and that's a good thing.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.537
-[ As Trump ]
The ratings were incredible.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.772
People are spending
a lot more time inside

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.207
watching TV for some reason.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.710
[ Normal voice ] It sucks so
hard that we have a president

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.579
who says things like
"We had a good slot."

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:29.682
He's bored by coronavirus,
but he loves TV.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.250
[ As Trump ] We're hoping in the
fall they put me on

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:35.087
after "This Is Us."
That'd be a hell of a lead-in.

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:36.956
[ Normal voice ] Also,
of course the ratings were good.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.590
People are locked inside
with nothing to watch,

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.960
desperate for information
about the out-of-control virus

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.161
you failed to stop.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.397
Ratings for "Wheel of Fortune"
would be up, too,

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.299
if Pat Sajak
went on a killing spree

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.534
and announced his next victims
via puzzle.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.169
Pat, I'd like to solve.

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:52.705
"You're next,
Dan from Rochester!"

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:55.507
[ Upbeat game show-style
music plays ]

00:02:55.507 --> 00:02:57.143
of course, Trump doesn't
actually care about

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.645
the deadly virus
that's spreading.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.312
He wants to resume the briefings

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:01.681
so he can do
what he always does --

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.850
whine about how unfairly
he's been treated,

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.018
threaten his political opponents
with state violence,

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:07.654
fight with reporters,

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:10.122
and speculate wildly
about dumb new treatments

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:12.625
until Dr. Fauci
covers his entire face.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.194
[ As Trump ]
Fauci, what if you -- and, yeah,

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.530
I'm just blue skying here --

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.732
ate a battery
and took a bath in Pepto-Bismol?

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.835
Would that cure the virus,
Fauci?

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:25.605
Fauci, why are you
wearing so many masks?

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.373
[ Normal voice ] So, Trump
is bored with the pandemic.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.908
And you can tell he's bored

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:31.277
from what he's been choosing
to focus on instead --

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.912
Beans and trucks.

00:03:33.912 --> 00:03:37.149
-On a day when 941 people
died of the coronavirus

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:40.753
in this country, this is what is
front of mind for the president,

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:41.954
beans.

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:44.022
The president
giving an endorsement to Goya

00:03:44.022 --> 00:03:46.959
a day after his daughter
Ivanka Trump did the same,

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:50.062
weighing into this bizarre
culture war

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:53.165
after Goya's CEO was criticized
on social media

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:55.334
for effusively praising
the president.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.436
-During an official event at the
White House,

00:03:57.436 --> 00:03:59.639
it became a photo op
for the president,

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.607
looking to move past
the pandemic

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.509
and look toward
the November election,

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:05.211
the president claiming
the biggest threat

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.046
to this country is his rival,

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.515
Democratic presidential nominee,
Joe Biden.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.184
The event turned into
a campaign-style rally.

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:14.787
The president had pickup trucks
and giant weights

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.189
symbolizing government
regulation,

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:20.893
the president only mentioning
the coronavirus once.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.328
-On the same day the U.S.
set another daily record

00:04:23.328 --> 00:04:24.964
with 75,000 new cases,

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.231
the president was playing
with trucks

00:04:26.231 --> 00:04:28.467
on the White House lawn
like he was lured into

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:29.835
one of those Chevy commercials.

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:32.071
[ As Trump ] JD Power, isn't
he part of the deep state?

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.906
[ Normal voice ] This looks like
one of those summer replacement

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.775
game shows where if you get
an answer wrong,

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:38.043
Ellen DeGeneres
drops a truck on you.

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:40.579
At what point can we consider
an obsession with trucks

00:04:40.579 --> 00:04:42.849
a disqualifying attribute
for a president?

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:45.718
I mean, adults are allowed to
have whatever hobbies they want.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.186
But if Bill Clinton had shown up

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.921
to every press conference
with a Tamagotchi,

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.324
Republicans definitely would've
impeached him a second time.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.524
[ As Bill Clinton ]
Now, if you excuse me,

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:54.627
I got to go feed
this little fella.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.562
[ Normal voice ] I mean, having
a president obsessed with trucks

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.931
is like having a president
obsessed with trains.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.966
Ayeh!

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.602
Amid a national health crisis
and record unemployment,

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:04.804
the federal government led by

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.973
a bored and sadistic president
has abandoned us.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.641
They simply do not care

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:11.176
about the 140,000 Americans
who have died,

00:05:11.176 --> 00:05:13.045
the tens of millions
who have lost jobs,

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:14.847
the 5 million who have lost
health insurance,

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:18.350
or the 23 million who face
eviction in the coming months.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.152
This is the result of decades

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:22.921
of conservative governance
that has raided the Treasury

00:05:22.921 --> 00:05:24.657
to doll out billions
in defense spending

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.325
and tax cuts for the wealthy,

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:28.160
while hollowing out
everything else.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.763
Now we have a pudding-brained
infomercial salesman,

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.598
who's more interested
in what happens

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.100
to a dead Confederate general

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.534
than a living
middle school teacher,

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:38.003
trying to convince us
that statues and graffiti

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:39.539
are more important
than a pandemic

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.807
that's caused massive suffering.

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:43.276
And even when he was asked
point blank

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.445
about the record number
of new cases

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:47.813
by Fox's Chris Wallace
this weekend,

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:49.248
Trump basically shrugged.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.917
-I'm going to do you a favor

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.985
because I'm sure a lot of people
listening right now

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:56.455
are going to say, Trump,
he tries to play it down,

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:58.257
he tries to make it
not seem as serious as it is.

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.892
-I'm not playing.
No. This is very serious.

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:03.363
-75,000 cases a day.
-Show me the death chart.

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.596
-Well,
I don't have the death chart.

00:06:04.596 --> 00:06:06.032
-Well, the death chart
is much more important.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:10.002
-But I can tell you the death
chart is a thousand cases a day.

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:12.805
-Excuse me. It's all too much.
It shouldn't be one case.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:15.507
It came from China. They
should've never let it escape.

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:18.310
They should've never let it out.
But it is what it is.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.846
-"It is what it is"
is a fine thing to hear --

00:06:20.846 --> 00:06:23.816
from a drinking buddy
as he promises you

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:26.518
that in time,
you will forget about Denise.

00:06:26.518 --> 00:06:28.554
But when the "it" is a pandemic

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:31.523
and the guy saying it is the
president, that's the problem.

00:06:31.523 --> 00:06:33.158
Had FDR
responded to Pearl Harbor

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:34.793
with a "[Bleep] Happens"
t-shirt,

00:06:34.793 --> 00:06:36.428
we'd probably feel different
about him today.

00:06:36.428 --> 00:06:39.865
We certainly wouldn't honor him
with the finest strip of road

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:42.835
along the East River
that's ever existed.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.570
Also, I love that Wallace
started out by saying,

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.738
"I'm going to do you a favor,"

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.506
and then Trump immediately
interrupts him.

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:50.075
That's how bad
a strategist he is.

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:51.877
Someone says,
"I'm going to do you a favor,"

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:54.146
you freeze like a squirrel
in a park

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:55.381
until you find out the favor.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.182
You don't start an argument.

00:06:57.182 --> 00:07:00.118
Second, it's not reassuring
when presented with evidence

00:07:00.118 --> 00:07:02.121
of a rapidly spreading disease,

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.723
your answer is,
"Show me the death chart."

00:07:04.723 --> 00:07:07.160
You know, 'cause that implies

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:08.828
there are enough deaths
for a chart.

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:11.029
In fact, if you work
in any office setting

00:07:11.029 --> 00:07:13.499
and you have death charts lying
around, something isn't right.

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:14.933
"Hey, Brad, regional sales

00:07:14.933 --> 00:07:16.168
are looking really good this
quarter."

00:07:16.168 --> 00:07:17.403
"That's fantastic, Linda.

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.037
Hey, would you hand me
the death chart,

00:07:19.037 --> 00:07:21.173
you know, the big one
that folds out?"

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:23.976
In fact, if this interview
revealed anything,

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:25.678
it's that the president
is far less concerned

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:27.880
with the deadly virus
sweeping through this nation

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:32.351
than he is with proving that he
supposedly did well on a test

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.553
designed to detect
cognitive defects

00:07:34.553 --> 00:07:36.155
that he constantly brags about.

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:38.057
Except this time
he was challenged by the host

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:41.527
Chris Wallace in a way he
obviously was not expecting.

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:44.430
-Let's take a test.
Let's take a test right now.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.899
Let's go down,
Joe and I will take a test.

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:49.368
Let him take the same test
that I took.

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:51.103
-Incidentally,
I took the test, too,

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:52.938
when I heard that you passed it.
-Yeah. How did you do?

00:07:52.938 --> 00:07:54.640
-Well,
it's not the hardest test.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.675
It has a picture that says,
"What's that?

00:07:56.675 --> 00:07:58.677
And it's an elephant.
-No, no, no. You see,

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:00.112
that's all misrepresentation.

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:01.013
-Well,
that's what it was on the Web.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:02.648
-It's all misrepresentation.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:05.050
Because, yes, the first
few questions are easy.

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.252
But I'll bet you couldn't even
answer the last five questions.

00:08:07.252 --> 00:08:08.454
I'll bet you couldn't.

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:09.922
They get very hard,
the last few questions.

00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:12.157
-Well, one of them was "Count
back from a hundred by seven."

00:08:12.157 --> 00:08:16.428
-And let me tell you,
you couldn't answer --

00:08:16.428 --> 00:08:19.332
-All right, what's the question?
-...many of the questions.

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.933
I'd get you the test.
I'd like to give it.

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:22.067
-Here's a question that should

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:23.769
be on Trump's next
cognitive test.

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:27.340
Name one question
from your last cognitive test.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.908
If you're going to constantly
brag about how well you did,

00:08:29.908 --> 00:08:32.878
you should at least be able
to say one of the questions.

00:08:32.878 --> 00:08:34.246
If you come home
and tell your parents

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:36.548
you aced your driving test
and they asked you what you did,

00:08:36.548 --> 00:08:39.218
you can't just shrug and say,
"I dunno, car stuff."

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:41.186
Because then they're going to
know you skipped it

00:08:41.186 --> 00:08:43.055
and had your buddy print out
a fake ID.

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:44.756
Also, I don't know
what's more alarming,

00:08:44.756 --> 00:08:47.759
that Trump even had to take
this test in the first place

00:08:47.759 --> 00:08:50.495
or how proud he is
with how he did.

00:08:50.495 --> 00:08:54.599
It's possible this is
the first test he ever passed

00:08:54.599 --> 00:08:55.834
that he took himself.

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:58.704
He probably paid an MIT student
to come with him,

00:08:58.704 --> 00:09:00.773
but then when he saw how easy it
was, sent him home.

00:09:00.773 --> 00:09:02.975
[ As Trump ] Elephant?
Well, I know what that is.

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:04.910
Get out of here, Poindexter.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:06.211
I'm not paying you, Poindexter.

00:09:06.211 --> 00:09:07.679
The deal was
if you took the test.

00:09:07.679 --> 00:09:09.414
Good news, I wasn't
going to pay you anyway.

00:09:09.414 --> 00:09:11.116
Don't be sad, Poindexter.

00:09:11.116 --> 00:09:12.551
[ Normal voice ]
I genuinely can't believe

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:14.286
this was a real exchange that
happened at the White House.

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:17.689
If you read this transcript
without any names attached,

00:09:17.689 --> 00:09:20.492
you'd think they were doctors'
notes from a psych ward.

00:09:20.492 --> 00:09:22.194
Also, there is no [bleep] way

00:09:22.194 --> 00:09:24.330
Trump can count backwards
from 100 by sevens.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.166
The money I would pay
to see him try that.

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:31.136
[ As Trump ] 100,
and then you're into the 90s.

00:09:31.136 --> 00:09:35.274
Some people say 95.
Some people say 92.

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:37.109
I had a guy come up to me
the other day.

00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:40.546
Big guy, tough guy,
tears in his eyes,

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:43.915
and he said, "Sir,
I think it's 91."

00:09:43.915 --> 00:09:47.786
